From: Ryan McClelland <rymcclel@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 07 Nov 2026 21:23:16 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] RenderingServer: hand the main RenderingDevice back to the main
 thread when the render thread ends

With the Separate thread model, _assign_mt_ids makes the main
RenderingDevice current on the render thread ("the main RD is created on
the main thread"). finish() stops that thread and sets server_thread back
to MAIN_ID, but leaves the RD current on the dead thread. The display
server then frees the RD on the main thread, ~RenderingDevice calls
finalize(), and its ERR_RENDER_THREAD_GUARD fails:

  ERROR: This function (finalize) can only be called from the render thread.
  ERROR: 7 RID allocations of type RenderingDevice::Texture were leaked at exit.

finalize() returns before freeing anything, so every RID the RD still owns
is reported leaked. Make the RD current on the main thread again once the
render thread has finished, mirroring _assign_mt_ids. Measured on Windows
(Vulkan, Forward+): the error and the leak report are gone; the default
thread model is unaffected.
---
diff --git a/servers/rendering/rendering_server_default.cpp b/servers/rendering/rendering_server_default.cpp
index 49b80b10b6..0c5984ca43 100644
--- a/servers/rendering/rendering_server_default.cpp
+++ b/servers/rendering/rendering_server_default.cpp
@@ -297,6 +297,14 @@ void RenderingServerDefault::finish() {
 			server_task_id = WorkerThreadPool::INVALID_TASK_ID;
 		}
 		server_thread = Thread::MAIN_ID;
+		// The render thread made the main RD current on itself (_assign_mt_ids).
+		// It is gone now, and the display server frees the RD on this thread:
+		// without handing it back, ~RenderingDevice's finalize() fails its
+		// render-thread guard and returns early, leaking every RID it owns.
+		RenderingDevice *rd = RenderingDevice::get_singleton();
+		if (rd) {
+			rd->make_current();
+		}
 	} else {
 		_finish();
 	}
